From d4e043dd5fbb3ae35c9fd54f7f31f12527d72c27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Paras <ThomasParas87@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:43:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(patterns): add upcloud_api_token, configcat_sdk_key,
 hackclub_ai_api_key, chief_tools_access_token, rainforest_pay_api_key

Round 2 of the 2026-10-05 weekly batch, formats verified against vendor
sources:

- upcloud_api_token (cloud.py, critical, 0.95): 'ucat_' + 26-char ULID
  (Crockford base32, first char 0-7). Vendor guide example + MIT Go SDK test.
- configcat_sdk_key (devops.py, LOW, 0.95): 'configcat-sdk-1/' + 22 + '/' + 22
  base64url, per the vendor SDK's isValidSdkKey(). Legacy unprefixed 22/22
  form deliberately not matched.
- hackclub_ai_api_key (ai.py, high, 0.95): 'sk-hc-v1-' + 64 lowercase hex
  (two dash-stripped randomUUIDs, vendor api.tsx; format facts only).
  Disjoint from openai_api_key.
- chief_tools_access_token (devops.py, high, 0.90): ctp_/ctt_/cto_/ctr_ +
  36-248 base62 with at least one digit. Prefixes per vendor docs, body per
  the MIT random-tokens PARSE_REGEX.
- rainforest_pay_api_key (payment.py, critical, 0.90): (sbx_)?apikey_ + 64
  lowercase hex, per vendor API reference. Left guard keeps it out of Paddle
  pdl_live_apikey_/pdl_sdbx_apikey_ keys (non-collision test).

Skipped: Devin service user token (cog_) - vendor docs give only the prefix;
the 52-char shape comes from an alphabet-sequence README placeholder.

All literals SYNTHETIC with split prefixes; vendor examples pinned as
known_test_values. TruffleHog not consulted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
